A||||5||Bluebottlejunky||Take out the Alt.||||1||
Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||03-06-2001||11:45 PM||||What is the easiest way to take out the Alt. on an 85 GT 4sp? I have heard to go through the wheel well?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85' GT 4sp||||reg||1
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||03-07-2001||01:59 AM||||take it out the top.  The only way to take it out through the wheel well is if you take the cv shaft out.  Take the top engine brace (dog bone) off at the engine side, and rotate it up and out of the way.  The engine will fall back toward the firewall, Take the passenger wheel off to access the lower bolt easily, then remove the upper bolt.  Rotate the alternator so you can access the 10mm nut that holds the power wire on and undo the plug.  Have a friend push the engine a bit and squeeze it out past the exhaust manifold and out the top.  I had to do this to mine yesterday, but I broke the upper bolt off, its really hard to remove it with the bracket still attached to it.  I had to take a cut off wheel and cut a chunk out of the bracket to remove the alt from it, then remove the bracket then the alt.  And my belts still squeal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||03-07-2001||08:50 AM||||I take the alt out of my 85SE v-6 4spd thru the bottom without much trouble. No need to remove the alt  bracket from the engine.  Remove the top pivot bolt from the top and the slider bolt from the bottom.  Be sure and disconnect the battery negative cable first.  There is a lot of energy at the cable connection at the alt.<P> My 85 GT auto is a different story.  It has to come out the top after removing the strut bracket and cooling tubes.<P>I'd suggest getting the belt tension adjusting tool from JC Whitney (around $4.00 US).  It surely helps tightening the belts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||03-07-2001||09:41 AM||||I second that. Taking it out the bottom is much easier.||||reg||1
Z||000004||PatrickB||03-07-2001||10:10 AM||||I have an 86 GT 4 speed and I dropped it out of the bottom without any trouble at all.  Didnt have to take anything apart.||||reg||14
Z||000005||rogergarrison||03-07-2001||12:18 PM||||Ive changed mine 3 times so im an expert on V6 alt. I take off the cooling tube by the alternator, remove the tension bolt and belt, take out the mounting bolt and drop it down and unhook wiring. then just turn it till it drops out. I can change mine in 20 mins now||||reg||1
